    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve for the product of the two numbers, let's denote the two numbers as \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). Given that the least common multiple (LCM) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 36 and the greatest common divisor (GCD) of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is 6, we can use the relationship between the LCM, GCD, and the product of the two numbers:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nCalculating the left-hand side:\n\n\\[\n216 = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
